                After each LLM call, DeepDoc runs a Python-side repair pipeline: code fence fixup,
                Mermaid diagram normalization, internal link rewriting, frontmatter description cleanup,
                and HTML code block normalization. Then a validation pass checks section coverage,
                file grounding, route accuracy, runtime/config/integration grounding, and hallucinated
                paths or symbols. On failure the LLM is reprompted with quality feedback (up to 3 retries
                with exponential backoff). Pages that still fail hard checks — provider truncation or hallucinated
                file paths — are reported as invalid. <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Nothing broken ever reaches disk.</strong>
